mb-owned-exceptions
-------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code, data,
fixtures, labels or weights.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
John J. O'Hare.
"Owned Edits to a Shared Decision Rule: Learning Private Exceptions as
Typed, Gated, Withdrawable Weight Edits".
arXiv:2611.15917, v1, submitted 11 Nov 2026. Primary category cs.LG,
cross-listed cs.CY.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.15917
Paper licence: CC0 1.0, https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
(as linked on the abs page).

Upstream repository
-------------------
None. The abs page links no method repository, and the paper says the two
other public repositories of the author's group contain neither the
compiler, the typed learner nor the acceptance test. Nothing was cloned,
installed or run.

Method only: the idea of a frozen published rule plus owned edits, each a
typed declaration (subject, scope, form, size) proposed only when the
owner's records pass a selection-aware evidence gate, re-derived by an
acceptance body into units reserved for the owner, and withdrawable
exactly; and the author's remark that on a rule-only base a table of owned
exceptions makes the same decisions. The domain, the rule, the typed space,
the gate threshold (a union bound over the typed space, not the paper's
Monte Carlo p-value), the integer unit encoding, the fixtures, the oracle
and the tests are this sketch's own. The abstract and parts of sections
2.1, 2.3 to 2.5 and 9.6 of the arXiv HTML were read; the PDF was not; no
network was trained and no model was run. The paper's claims appear only in
paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked UNVERIFIED.
